The first measures how many edges are in agreement between the estimated tree, T^\hat{T}, and the true tree, TT. The second measures the agreement of centrality measures for the nodes in each graph and “a change in centrality can be understood as a drift of the node away from (or toward) the core of the network” ([Donnat and Holmes, 2018](https://arxiv.org/html/2208.01208v2#bib.bib15)).

